{"id": 10, "ts": 1781179795.7405543, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the strong case made for Candidate\u202fB, especially the clear evidence of conscientiousness, stress resilience, and technical competence. However, we still lack any concrete information on B\u2019s attention to numeric data\u2014an essential aspect for flight\u2011planning accuracy\u2014so that remains an open risk.\nTurning to Candidate\u202fD, the notes show they \u201crespond to unexpected events adequately,\u201d \u201cconcentrate very well,\u201d and \u201csolve problems extremely well,\u201d while also \u201ctaking responsibility seriously.\u201d Those traits align well with operational reliability, decision quality, and responsibility. Yet the same candidate is described as a \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d and has a \u201chot temper,\u201d which could undermine crew cooperation, professional communication, and stress resilience in the cockpit.\nGiven the current evidence, I still lean toward Candidate\u202fB as the provisional lead, but I recommend we probe Candidate\u202fD\u2019s temperament further\u2014specifically how the hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all perception have manifested in team settings\u2014before we finalize our decision."}
